    {
      "id": "lesson-browser-window-basics",
      "courseId": "course-browser",
      "moduleId": "group-sliding-windows",
      "slug": "lesson-browser-window-basics",
      "title": "Sliding Window Basics",
      "type": "LESSON",
      "visibility": "PUBLIC",
      "paymentAccess": "FREE",
      "publicationStatus": "PUBLISHED",
      "required": true,
      "order": 3,
      "body": "# Sliding Window Basics\n\nA sliding window is an algorithmic technique used to perform operations on a specific window size of an array or sequence, such as finding the maximum sum of $k$ consecutive elements.\n\nInstead of recalculating the entire window sum from scratch ($O(n \\times k)$), the window slides by one element:\n1. Add the incoming element entering the window.\n2. Subtract the outgoing element leaving the window.\n\nThis reduces the overall time complexity to $O(n)$.\n"
    },
